ence": "medium", "notes": ["No expert rater lists this race; fundamentals point clearly one way (post-redistricting), so it is treated as safe for that party."]}, "overview": "Utah's 1st District became markedly more Democratic after redistricting, and Democrat Ben McAdams enters the general election as a heavy favorite over Republican Riley Owen. McAdams has raised roughly $2.3 million to Owen's $133,000, with outside groups spending $2.7 million to support him and nothing to oppose him. A September poll of likely voters showed McAdams ahead by 42 points, and prediction markets put his win odds around 96%.\n\nThe candidates' debates emphasized broad agreement between two moderates, with disagreements mainly on debt and the economy. Given the district's 12-point Democratic lean, a favorable environment for the party, and the financial imbalance, the race is rated Safe Democratic, with an expected margin in the mid-to-high twenties.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9908, "margin": 20.9}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.99, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9893, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9909, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9895, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9899, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9906, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9886, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9895, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9907, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.99, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9979, "margin": 28.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9958, "margin": 26.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.997, "margin": 27.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9991, "margin": 28.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9988, "margin": 27.0}]}